          "concern": "The replacement helper changes from one replacement triple to a list of triples; unchanged values should not append a malformed or unnecessary operation.",
          "response": "The selected implementation documents the exact extend caller contract. An existing scoped shared lesson already covers this helper/caller pairing, so it is reused rather than duplicated.",
          "applied": "mk_gecko_rev_replacement returns an empty list or a nested replacement triple, and each caller uses extend. The final merge replacement collection also receives extend. Frozen helper/caller preserves that shape.",
          "outcome": "This is a data-shape and caller contract, not an append/extend style preference. No Treescript invocation or replacement-file mutation was run."
        },
        {
          "concern": "A configured regex has an unclosed group, and the transform unconditionally reads an optional GECKO_HEAD_REV key.",
          "response": "The main bug describes the missing-parenthesis follow-up, later backout and explicit later KeyError diagnosis for central-to-beta. It then proposes a placeholder workaround while requesting a Treescript fix. These later reasons are distinct from the first July breakage.",
          "applied": "Selected671 still includes the malformed comm-bump-esr128 base pattern and direct GECKO_HEAD_REV lookup. Retained focused later source corrects the group; the later reland/workaround creates a replaceable placeholder for main-to-beta. Existing source-derived regex and optional-key claims are reused, with later discussion gaps preserved.",
